      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-24T02:44:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not? You are making a change to the android 12 trusty Linux driver and FF-A is \"STRONGLY RECOMMENDED\" by the android 12 cdd: https://source.android.com/compatibility/12/android-12-cdd",
      "parentUuid": "63f49361_e90cc10f",
      "revId": "684febe23537b8ad6968561f195cc384a6143118",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5d65b1b_1c519432",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1206463
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-24T02:55:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Arve,\n\nThanks for your reply! Some of our SoCs are based on \"old\" ARM architecture and target for low-end markets, FF-A are not supported on these platforms.\n\nThis commit will allocate memory based on the trusty api level, it makes sure we will not decrease the log buffer size even for old trusty api level.",
      "parentUuid": "9812e23a_3d76d45f",
      "revId": "684febe23537b8ad6968561f195cc384a6143118",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "64b8f905_9eee641e",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-24T03:04:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FF-A is not a hardware feature. It is how trusty allows sharing memory in a way that is compatible with a hypervisor (currently only in the non-secure world). While the a low-end device might not have a hypervisor, skipping FF-A support has implications beyond that new features loadable apps depend on it.",
      "parentUuid": "f5d65b1b_1c519432",
      "revId": "684febe23537b8ad6968561f195cc384a6143118",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04ed8535_c0bde9d3",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1206463
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-24T04:39:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes. For these low-end platforms we don\u0027t have plan to support FF-A but do have plan to support Android 12. For loadable apps, actually we have modified the apploader to make it allocate physical continuous shared memory in such case so it can work.\n\nAs this driver still supports old trusty api as compat so keep the same log buffer size seems reasonable.",
      "parentUuid": "64b8f905_9eee641e",
      "revId": "684febe23537b8ad6968561f195cc384a6143118",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
